B.bc0=new A.T("YOUR TRIBUTARY",B.n)
B.bc1=new A.T("","The Danes and the Norwegians start at war with every other realm, with war-fleets already on the coast.")
B.bc2=new A.T("Wales and Scotland"," can instead hold every province they started with and win 18 more.")
B.bc4=new A.T("The coalition:"," from turn 6, if you come close to victory, the other realms make peace among themselves and all go to war with you until you fall back. The panel at the top left says when; on Hard it comes sooner. It can turn on a runaway rival too.")
B.bc5=new A.T("AT PEACE",B.v)
B.bc6=new A.T("","Attacking or pillaging a realm you are not at war with declares war \u2014 but not while a peace still holds.")
B.bc8=new A.T("","Then they pay 50% more tax and give more men, and your armies fight 10% harder among them.")
B.bc9=new A.T("Walls:"," assault a fortified province (its defenders fight 30% harder per wall level), or besiege it \u2014 it falls in a few turns if your army stays beside it.")
B.bca=new A.T("Pillage"," a province your army stands in or borders: not your own, not one guarded by another realm's army, and only if your men outnumber its levies, who fight back.")
B.bcb=new A.T("Light raid, heavy raid or full pillage:"," the harder you strike, the more gold and the more ruin. It takes the army's whole turn, and starts a war if you were not at war.")
B.bce=new A.T("Danegeld:"," when the Danes are much stronger than you and their hosts stand at your border, they demand half your treasury (at least 100 gold) for 8 turns of peace. It only buys time: when the peace runs out, they come back. East Anglia, the land they came for, is never offered terms. Playing the Danes, you can demand Danegeld yourself.")
B.bch=new A.T("Attacks are orders"," fought when you end the turn. Each army fights one battle a turn, and armies sent against the same province fight as one host. A realm's province with no army in it is still defended by the levies it musters.")
B.bcj=new A.T("","Playing Scotland, you start with a 6-turn truce with the Norwegians.")
B.bcn=new A.T("Recruit more troops",!1)
B.bco=new A.T("When turn 8 ends,"," the Danes' Great Heathen Army lands on East Anglia's coast \u2014 the kingdom they come to take (anywhere on England's east coast when you play East Anglia).")
B.bcp=new A.T("Tap an army"," to select it. Green provinces are ones it can march into \u2014 your own or an ally's. Red ones marked with crossed swords can be attacked.")
B.bcq=new A.T(null,"They refuse.")
B.bcs=new A.T("Gold"," comes from taxes \u2014 the more people, the more gold \u2014 and from markets, ports and mines. Manpower comes from your people, and more from barracks.")
B.bct=new A.T("Peace:"," a realm at war with you makes peace when it is losing \u2014 weaker than you, and none of its homeland in your hands. Peace lasts 8 turns, and neither side may attack while it holds.")
B.bcv=new A.T("","Your armies join only when one marches onto another, or when you press Combine.")
B.bcx=new A.T("2 moves a turn:"," march twice, or march and then attack. Marching into highland takes both moves.")
B.bcz=new A.T(null,"No active game")
B.bcB=new A.T("","Now and then an event card asks you to choose.")
B.bcD=new A.T("","The handshake button at the top right opens the realms of Britain.")
