B.bcN=new A.T("When you are attacked,"," SALLY OUT is your charge, and ABANDON gives up the province to save your men: its levies fall back to a neighbouring province you hold.")
B.bcP=new A.T("","You lose if another realm wins first, or if you lose all your land and armies. The panel at the top left shows how far you have come and the rival closest to winning.")
B.bcR=new A.T("Rule 35 provinces.","Every realm wins this way. The land of realms that pay you tribute counts too.")
B.bcS=new A.T("","Each turn is one season, four to a year, starting in spring 793.")
B.bcT=new A.T("","Your starting provinces also build on their own, with part of your spare gold.")
B.asX=new A.T(null,B.h)
B.bcU=new A.T(B.lk,B.lj)
B.bcZ=new A.T("Battles are live."," Troops and morale fall round by round. CHARGE! is a gamble: it can break a wavering enemy, but against a strong, steady line many of your men fall. Pulling back is free before the lines meet (CALL OFF) and costly after (RETREAT). A side whose morale reaches zero breaks and is cut down.")
